    "notes": [
      {
        "x": 10200,
        "y": 120,
        "text": "R10 wood-well  PURPOSE: the dark under everything, where the dead go, and the threshold. In from the silk hall's floor (one way)"
      },
      { "x": 9000, "y": 360, "text": "THE ROOT STAIR: dark ledges stepping down west, glide gaps" },
      {
        "x": 9740,
        "y": 480,
        "text": "a root mass over L1's west half (80 clear): walk under it, no jump. THE POGO-WICK just under the lip: drop, down-cut it, it snuffs and bounces her on to L2"
      },
      { "x": 9500, "y": 1100, "text": "a miss: the catch puts her back on L1" },
      {
        "x": 8500,
        "y": 400,
        "text": "a lit landing (L2): W-chute over it (no dangler over a fall-return point)"
      },
      { "x": 7500, "y": 600, "text": "a lit landing (L3): W-pocket over it" },
      { "x": 6560, "y": 1080, "text": "E0: the stair's foot; drop into the nest" },
      {
        "x": 5700,
        "y": 700,
        "text": "gaps 448 / 480 / 448: each a plain jump from its open lip; the first also a walk-off glide"
      },
      {
        "x": 4000,
        "y": 1500,
        "text": "THE NEST: a low root hall where every carriers' trail ends, piled with wings; two lit pockets, a dangler over each"
      },
      {
        "x": 3880,
        "y": 1580,
        "text": "THE WINDOW (a held beat): through the slot in the den's wall, the old burrback asleep on its carpet of wings"
      },
      {
        "x": 3640,
        "y": 2040,
        "text": "P-den at the den's door: a fade re-forms her here, 5 s from the fight; a jump (256) back up to the nest"
      },
      {
        "x": 2000,
        "y": 1560,
        "text": "THE DEN under the oak: its ceiling the plug (the column's foot). The old burrback; W-den high in the west half, off the column's line (caught only, from a jump); the taproot (rams stun on it; she walks under)"
      },
      {
        "x": 2560,
        "y": 1300,
        "text": "its death sets wood-old-burrback-down: the plug falls, the moon column pours in, the claws where it died (glade, shut till then)"
      },
      {
        "x": 2580,
        "y": 900,
        "text": "the climb-out is the column: both faces, catch ledges, the root step at the top; up through the oak's root mesh (sets wood-climbout)"
      },
      {
        "x": 600,
        "y": 400,
        "text": "THE WEST ROOT ROAD (claws): the tunnel from the nest's shaft west over the den, across the column; W-road a find"
      },
      { "x": 3640, "y": 900, "text": "the nest's claw shaft up to the road" }
    ],
